# quests store snapshot (internal/quests)
# Built 2026-09-12 from PRE-migration code, sending what each site sends today:
# reward actor/observer and action actor RAW (no substitution),
# action observer through textutil.SubstituteTokens with the player as {actor}.
# dimensions: quest id x rewards | trigger<i>|action<j>[|sequence|action<k>...] x key

quest|2|rewards|actor => The shaman inclines its fungus-crowned head, the closest thing to a bow its mutated frame allows. You are not welcome here. But you are tolerated. That is more than any surface-dweller has been given in living memory.
quest|2|rewards|observer => A low, guttural call passes from the shaman into the dark of the deeper tunnels. Something has shifted.
quest|4|rewards|actor => Tessara examines the papers from the purse with a grim expression, then folds them carefully into her report stack. 'Names, routes, schedules. The wardens at Watchers Crossing will want to see this.' She reaches into a pouch and produces a clay token, pressing it into your hand. 'You have earned this. Every warden on these roads will know what it means.'
quest|4|rewards|observer => Tessara nods to herself as she reads through the confiscated documents, already composing her report.
quest|5|rewards|actor => Tolva pages through the ledger with practiced speed, her lips pressed thin. 'Just as I thought. No writ of authority, no commission from Thornwall, no charter. He set this toll up himself.' She closes the book firmly. 'I will send this to the magistrate with my next supply order. You have done this settlement a service.' She slides a wooden token across the counter.
quest|5|rewards|observer => Tolva examines the ledger with grim satisfaction, already composing a letter in her head.
quest|6|rewards|actor => Harn exhales slowly when you confirm the report is on its way. 'That is all I can do. If they see the numbers, what the stone costs, what the masons charge, what happens if that crack reaches the keystone, they will understand. The toll is not greed. It is the only thing keeping that bridge standing.' He produces a stamped receipt. 'For your crossing. You have earned it, and then some.'
quest|6|rewards|observer => Harn nods with quiet relief, adjusting the ledger on his counter.
quest|7|rewards|actor => Dorn examines the pest sample with a grim expression, then sets it down carefully. 'Bigger than they should be. The fallow field is feeding them, all that untended root growth, it is a paradise for vermin.' He looks toward Thornwall's walls. 'Gareth was a good farmer. The tax took everything. And now the rest of us pay for it in different coin.' He reaches into a pouch. 'This is not much, but it is honest.'
quest|7|rewards|observer => Dorn nods slowly, the weight of the situation evident in his weathered face.
quest|7|trigger1|action0|actor => The pest goes still. To search it for a sample, type loot corpse.
quest|8|rewards|actor => Velk listens to your report without interruption, his expression unreadable. When you finish, he makes a notation in the duty log. 'The case is closed. I will file it accordingly.' He does not ask for details beyond what you offered, and you get the sense that he has seen enough of these cases to know that the paperwork rarely captures the whole truth.
quest|8|rewards|observer => Velk makes a notation in the duty log and files the report.
quest|9|rewards|actor => The ledger's contents are damning in both directions. Whoever receives it will use it to their advantage, and the other side will suffer for it. Or perhaps the public airing of both parties' dishonesty will force a more honest arrangement. In Thornwall, optimism is a luxury, but sometimes the truth is enough.
quest|9|rewards|observer => The tithe ledger changes hands, and the balance of power shifts.
quest|10|rewards|actor => Marek pours you a drink on the house, the good stuff, from the bottle he keeps behind the keg. 'The guard cannot fix the taxes, but at least I will not have to pay two masters. That is something.' He glances toward the cellar stairs. 'While you were gone, I heard noises down there again. Something in the old drainage tunnels beneath the city. I have been meaning to look, but...' He trails off. 'Another time, perhaps. For now, drink.'
quest|10|rewards|observer => Marek pours a drink with visible relief, some of the tension leaving his shoulders.
quest|11|rewards|actor => You have chosen your path. The steppe will remember.
quest|12|rewards|actor => Sylara's eyes shine with quiet pride. The steppe wind swirls around you like a greeting, and you feel a new connection to the land, ancient, vast, and watchful. She presses a spirit fetish into your hands.
quest|13|rewards|actor => Rhett grins broadly, cradling the extracted crystal like a newborn. He disappears into his work for hours, and when he emerges, he holds a shield of pale blue crystal: the Windstone Aegis, forged in gratitude.
quest|13|rewards|observer => Rhett emerges from his camp, grinning, and presents a shield of pale blue crystal to his companion.
quest|14|rewards|actor => Guard Captain Velk nods with grim satisfaction. 'This ledger changes everything. Names, dates, amounts, enough to end careers and start trials. You have done Thornwall a real service.' He hands you a folded parchment bearing the Watch seal. 'A commendation. It may not buy you a drink, but it buys you goodwill with the guard.'
quest|14|rewards|observer => Velk hands over a sealed document with a look of grudging respect.
quest|14|trigger0|action0|actor => The opening past the grate leads only into the old drainage tunnels. You have no reason to go down there.
quest|14|trigger1|action1|actor => A tally stick, notched to record regular shipments. Someone is running goods through these tunnels on a schedule. The chalk arrows on the walls point south, deeper into the system.
quest|14|trigger2|action1|actor => You step into a well-lit chamber that serves as the nerve center of the smuggling operation. A man at the table looks up sharply. This must be the one in charge. A heavy iron strongbox sits beneath his table, locked tight. Whatever proof you need is probably in there.
quest|14|trigger3|action0|actor => The strongbox is open and empty. You have already taken the ledger.
quest|14|trigger4|action3|actor => You fit the brass key into the padlock and turn. The lock clicks open. Inside the strongbox you find a slim leather journal, a bribe ledger, filled with names, dates, and amounts paid to corrupt city officials. This is the evidence you need.
quest|14|trigger4|action4|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> unlocks the strongbox and pulls out a leather journal.
quest|14|trigger5|action0|actor => The strongbox is locked with a heavy brass padlock. You need a key.
quest|14|trigger6|action1|actor => Torvan Cresk falls. The strongbox key is still on his belt.
quest|14|trigger9|action1|actor => The strongbox is open and empty. Then your fingers find a false bottom, and under it Torvan's second copy of the bribe ledger.
quest|14|trigger10|action0|actor => The strongbox is open and empty. Guard Captain Velk has the ledger now.
quest|15|rewards|actor => Malk examines the crate, running his elongated fingers over the forced lock. 'This is the one. Everything accounted for, near enough.' He reaches into the cart and produces a small purse and presses it into your hand.
quest|15|rewards|observer => Malk examines the recovered freight crate with evident relief, already tallying his inventory.
quest|16|rewards|actor => Delia nods slowly, the practical assessment of someone who has weighed a solution and found it sound. 'You have a good eye for problems and their fixes. My worktable is yours whenever you need it. Come back any time.'
quest|16|rewards|observer => Delia's expression shifts from concern to quiet satisfaction as the herb supply problem is resolved.
quest|18|rewards|actor => What happened on the north road stays on the north road.
quest|18|trigger0|action1|actor => A rough bed of straw piled against the wall in the darkest corner of the barn, half covered by an old horse blanket. The straw is pressed flat where someone slept, and not long ago. A few dark hairs cling to the blanket, and beside it lies a withered apple core. Someone stayed here. Betta, out in the yard, must know who.
quest|18|trigger4|action2|actor => The agent goes down in the road and does not rise. Whoever sent this one will send another, and they will look harder at this stretch of road now. Betta will hear of it.
quest|19|rewards|actor => The lake-caves bounty is closed. A purse changes hands.
quest|19|rewards|observer => is paid out the lake-caves bounty.
quest|19|trigger0|action1|actor => The skitter-shrimp swarm has been broken. The lake-folk's nets will hold longer for it.
quest|19|trigger1|action1|actor => The drowned hunter is dead. The shallows are meaningfully safer.
quest|20|rewards|actor => Ulla unfolds the journal page slowly. She reads it twice. The second time she sets it on her knee and puts both hands flat over it for a long moment, as if to keep it from blowing away. When she looks up, her eyes are wet but steady for the first time in years.

'I knew it was something,' she says quietly. 'I knew it was something he could not say.'

She rises with effort and takes up a long wrapped bundle from beside the hearth: Elgar's hook-spear, the lake-iron bright and new. 'Brindle brought this to my door after you spoke with him. He finished it at last, twelve years late.' She places it in your hands without ceremony.

'It was meant for someone who would understand. He'd want it to be you.'
quest|20|rewards|observer => is given a long wrapped bundle by Ulla, who closes her hand over hers for a moment before letting go.
quest|20|trigger0|action1|actor => A long tight spiral inside an outer ring, scratched into the iron with a patient hand. The cuts are dark with age: old work, set where it would not be noticed by anyone who did not know to look. Not a Chrysalis sigil and not a Stillwater fish-mark. The same spiral is cut into the two stone pillars on the Temple Approach in town.
quest|20|trigger1|action1|actor => A long tight spiral inside an outer ring, scratched into the iron with a patient hand. The cuts are dark with age: old work, set where it would not be noticed by anyone who did not know to look. Not a Chrysalis sigil and not a Stillwater fish-mark. The same spiral is cut into the two stone pillars on the Temple Approach in town.
quest|20|trigger2|action1|actor => The two pillars that frame the Temple Approach carry the same spiral that Elgar scratched into his bench-vise, worked into the stone with patience and skill, far older than the temple behind them. The temple garden, south of the temple, may hold more of the same.
quest|20|trigger4|action1|actor => The buried marker beneath the crab-apple carries the same spiral. Older than the garden it sits in. Northwest of town, on a low rise, there is a circle of standing stones with an old chapel ruin just west of it. The symbol may appear there again.
quest|20|trigger5|action1|actor => The buried marker beneath the crab-apple carries the same spiral. Older than the garden it sits in. Northwest of town, on a low rise, there is a circle of standing stones with an old chapel ruin just west of it. The symbol may appear there again.
quest|20|trigger6|action1|actor => The buried marker beneath the crab-apple carries the same spiral. Older than the garden it sits in. Northwest of town, on a low rise, there is a circle of standing stones with an old chapel ruin just west of it. The symbol may appear there again.
quest|20|trigger7|action1|actor => The chapel altar carries the same spiral, the third site you have found. Back to the east, the Wardstone Circle has a carved altar slab at its centre. It may be the fourth.
quest|20|trigger8|action1|actor => The chapel altar carries the same spiral, the third site you have found. Back to the east, the Wardstone Circle has a carved altar slab at its centre. It may be the fourth.
quest|20|trigger9|action1|actor => The chapel altar carries the same spiral, the third site you have found. Back to the east, the Wardstone Circle has a carved altar slab at its centre. It may be the fourth.
quest|20|trigger10|action1|actor => The wardstone slab carries the spiral worn deep enough to set a finger into: the fourth site you have found. A worn channel runs from it straight toward the east. Stand at the circle's centre with the chapel ruin at your back, follow the channel with your eye, and the alignment is plain: the chapel, this slab, and on east past the north edge of the town, out under the lake, and down, somewhere only the lake caves can reach. The pillars and the garden marker lie south of the line, like signposts pointing to it.
quest|20|trigger11|action1|actor => The wardstone slab carries the spiral worn deep enough to set a finger into: the fourth site you have found. A worn channel runs from it straight toward the east. Stand at the circle's centre with the chapel ruin at your back, follow the channel with your eye, and the alignment is plain: the chapel, this slab, and on east past the north edge of the town, out under the lake, and down, somewhere only the lake caves can reach. The pillars and the garden marker lie south of the line, like signposts pointing to it.
quest|20|trigger12|action1|actor => The wardstone slab carries the spiral worn deep enough to set a finger into: the fourth site you have found. A worn channel runs from it straight toward the east. Stand at the circle's centre with the chapel ruin at your back, follow the channel with your eye, and the alignment is plain: the chapel, this slab, and on east past the north edge of the town, out under the lake, and down, somewhere only the lake caves can reach. The pillars and the garden marker lie south of the line, like signposts pointing to it.
quest|20|trigger13|action1|actor => The oilskin pouch holds a folded note in Elgar's hand, addressed to Brindle the smith. The note explains the spiral: the chapel, the wardstone circle and the deep sump beneath the lake lie on one line, and the marks at the temple point the way to it. Elgar wrote that he was going down alone because he could not wait for Brindle to finish the work he was doing. The note is dated the day he disappeared. A small black pearl and a curl of waxed line lie with it; you leave them where he set them. Brindle needs to know you found this.
quest|20|trigger15|action2|actor => Inside the buried wooden box: a single small carved kingfisher in dark wood, unmistakably Elgar's work, and a folded note in a different hand reading 'He was your brother. V.' The kingfisher is yours now. Bring it to Vella at the Healer's Cottage.
quest|20|trigger16|action2|actor => Inside the buried wooden box: a single small carved kingfisher in dark wood, unmistakably Elgar's work, and a folded note in a different hand reading 'He was your brother. V.' The kingfisher is yours now. Bring it to Vella at the Healer's Cottage.
quest|20|trigger17|action1|actor => There was another small carving wrapped beneath the first. You can take this one to Vella in place of the one you lost.
quest|20|trigger18|action2|actor => Inside the buried wooden box: a single small carved kingfisher in dark wood, unmistakably Elgar's work, and a folded note in a different hand reading 'He was your brother. V.' The kingfisher is yours now. Bring it to Vella at the Healer's Cottage.
quest|28|rewards|actor => Dewey's hand is steady on your shoulder, and his voice is warm, already a little proud. You are awake now, and the world is real.
quest|28|trigger5|action0|actor => You crouch for a closer look at the threshold-stone. Its surface is polished to a shine, hollowed at the center by every soul who ever woke here and stepped through. The fine lines around its edge are names, hundreds of them, small and neat, no two written alike. Toward the hollowed center the oldest have worn almost smooth, and one of them still reads Dewey.
quest|28|trigger6|action1|actor => You crouch for a closer look at the threshold-stone. Its surface is polished to a shine, hollowed at the center by every soul who ever woke here and stepped through. The fine lines around its edge are names, hundreds of them, small and neat, no two written alike. Toward the hollowed center the oldest have worn almost smooth, and one of them still reads Dewey.
quest|30|rewards|actor => Something under your skin settles into place, the way silt settles in still water. You are not quite who you were when you arrived. A small light waits in you now too: in any dark place, type cast glow.
quest|31|rewards|actor => Toke presses a small purse into your palm with his upper mouth still talking and the lower one already calling the next notice.
quest|31|trigger0|action1|actor => A tutor glances up from a slate as you enter. "Newly Opened. When the changes start and you want to know what is happening to you, this hall is where you come." Next, go to Coulee Provisions, south past Hub Square to Market Row and then east, and type list.
quest|31|trigger1|action1|actor => Trader Onna watches you weigh her wares. "The cotton shirt keeps the chill off and the coulee's teeth out. You have coin enough." Type buy cotton shirt.
quest|31|trigger2|action1|actor => Trader Onna nods as the coin changes hands. "A shirt won't turn a blade, but it beats bare skin. Put it on. Gear does nothing folded in your pack." Type equip cotton shirt.
quest|31|trigger3|action1|actor => You settle the shirt across your shoulders. That is the whole of it: buy the gear, wear the gear, and the coulee bites a little less. Next, find The Drowned Lantern: from Coulee Provisions go west twice.
quest|31|trigger4|action1|actor => The keeper of the Drowned Lantern tips you a nod as you step in. "First one is on the house -- the coulee's welcome. Rest while it is still being gentle with you." Now go back to Crier Toke in Hub Square, east and then north, and type talk toke.
quest|32|rewards|actor => Vorn turns your performance over in his head for a long moment, the way a smith eyes a finished blade for flaws. Then he nods once, short, like it costs him something. "Passable. You did not freeze, you did not panic, and you remembered to think between swings. That is more than most manage on the first day." He presses a few coins into your hand. "There is real work out in the wash. Ask me about it when you are ready."
quest|32|rewards|observer => Vorn nods at <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> with a gruff, brief approval.
quest|32|trigger0|action1|actor => Vorn has your measure now. Take up the cudgel: type wield cudgel. If it is already in your hand, first use remove cudgel.
quest|32|trigger1|action1|actor => The cudgel sits in your hand. Before you fight, size up the training dummy: type consider dummy.
quest|32|trigger2|action1|actor => Now you know what you face. Fight it: type attack dummy.
quest|32|trigger3|action1|actor => The training dummy shudders and goes still. Your arms remember the rhythm of it: weight, angle, follow through. A new dummy stands up soon. When it does, type kick dummy.
quest|32|trigger4|action1|actor => That is a special move. Now choose how much combat detail you see: type set combatverbosity full.
quest|32|trigger5|action1|actor => That is a special move. Now choose how much combat detail you see: type set combatverbosity full.
quest|32|trigger6|action1|actor => Your combat detail is set. Report to Drillmaster Vorn: type talk vorn.
quest|33|rewards|actor => Garve presses a purse into your hand and holds your gaze a moment longer than is strictly necessary, like someone revising his estimate upward. The leggings he slides from the pack beside him are well made, cut for movement, and they fit.
quest|33|trigger0|action1|actor => Garve has told you what the wash needs. Start with the scout. Go north to the Lower Wash and type attack scout.
quest|33|trigger1|action1|actor => The bandit scout goes down. A bandit's gear does not always survive the fight: type loot corpse to see what is left. Next is the squatter. From Squatter's Hollow, go east to the Cracked Cistern and type attack squatter.
quest|33|trigger2|action1|actor => The bandit squatter drops. Some of her gear may have survived the fight, so loot the corpse before you go. Then go back to Garve in Squatter's Hollow and type talk garve.
quest|34|rewards|actor => Garve hears you out without a word. Then he reaches behind him for a well-kept blade, turns it once in his good hand, and holds it out to you. "I took this off one of hers in the ambush. It belonged to the watch captain they killed for that tower. You took the tower, you keep it. It has changed owners by violence before, and it found a better one this time." He counts coin into your palm. "Whatever she was guarding is the coulee's question now, not hers."
quest|34|rewards|observer => Garve hands <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> a well-kept blade and a purse of coin.
quest|34|trigger0|action1|actor => The captain falls, and the watch room goes quiet. Take the news down to Garve: type talk garve when you reach him.
quest|34|trigger1|action1|actor => The fight leaves something behind in your arms and back: a settled, lasting strength, earned the hard way at the top of a tower.
quest|34|trigger2|action1|actor => The fight leaves something behind in your hands and feet: a settled, lasting quickness, earned the hard way at the top of a tower.
quest|35|rewards|actor => Rusk looks at you, not at the forge, with the measuring expression of a smith deciding whether a piece of iron is worth tempering. Then she nods once and presses a few coins into your hand with the finality of a door closing.
quest|35|rewards|observer => Rusk nods once and presses a few coins into <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi>'s hand.
quest|35|trigger0|action1|actor => Rusk has shown you the shape of it. Start with her stall: type list.
quest|35|trigger1|action1|actor => Those are Rusk's goods. The dagger needs an iron ingot and a leather strip. Type buy iron ingot.
quest|35|trigger2|action1|actor => You have an iron ingot. Now the grip. Type buy leather strip.
quest|35|trigger3|action1|actor => You have the leather strip. That is everything the dagger needs. At the forge, type craft iron dagger.
quest|35|trigger4|action1|actor => The iron dagger is yours, made at the forge. Show it to Rusk, or sell it to her if you would rather have the coin. Either way, type talk rusk after.
quest|36|rewards|actor => Ovell digs a worn leather pouch from his coat with the care of someone parting with something that has been useful. The quartz eye tracks you steadily while the other squints in the slope light. "You cleared it. Worked the vein. I did not know if you would come back." He presses the component pouch into your hands and curls your fingers around the strap. "Materials go in on their own once you wear it. Sort if you have loose ones already. And if you ever want to break a piece of kit back down, salvage it. The slope gives back what you put into it, mostly."
quest|36|trigger0|action1|actor => Ovell has told you what the slope needs. The scavenger first. Go north to the Lower Talus and type attack scavenger.
quest|36|trigger1|action1|actor => The scree scavenger goes still on the rock. Next is the talus lurker. In the Ore Pocket, type attack lurker.
quest|36|trigger2|action1|actor => The talus lurker drops back into the rock and does not rise. Now work the vein. In the Ore Pocket or on the Scree Field, type forage.
quest|36|trigger3|action1|actor => You work the exposed vein for whatever it will give. The seam is open to anyone now. Go back to Ovell in the Collapsed Cut and type talk ovell.
quest|36|trigger4|action1|actor => You pick through the rubble where the vein crosses the ore pocket. The seam is open to anyone now. Go back to Ovell, just east of here, and type talk ovell.
quest|37|rewards|actor => Ovell listens with his quartz eye half closed, as if he can hear the deep mine through the rock. When you finish he nods slowly. "Then the vein is yours." He talks you through how the dark ore folds into an edge until the shape of the recipe settles in your head, and he draws a dark blade from under his coat. "Keep that. The first of many." The long work of the slope has settled into your arms as a lasting strength.
quest|37|trigger0|action1|actor => The stone-blooded beast shudders, its fused hide cracking like cooling slag, and goes down for the last time. The deep mine is quiet. Climb back up to Ovell and type talk ovell.
quest|38|rewards|actor => Birna takes the empty vial back and turns it to the light, checking the film the salve left behind. The green-gold veining in her hands catches the same light. "Clean steep. You did not scorch the root. Most do, the first time." She tucks a pair of empty vials into your pack and presses a folded scrap of waxed paper after them. "The antidote formula. You will want it before the marsh teaches you why. Set your home here first, so you have somewhere to wake."
quest|38|rewards|observer => Birna inspects the empty vial, nods, and tucks a few things into the newcomer's pack.
quest|38|trigger0|action1|actor => Birna has shown you the shape of it. Start with her racks. Type list.
quest|38|trigger1|action1|actor => That is Birna's stock. A healing salve needs one glass vial and two healer's roots. Type buy glass vial.
quest|38|trigger2|action1|actor => The glass vial will hold the salve. Now the roots, two of them. Type buy 2 healer's root.
quest|38|trigger3|action1|actor => Two healer's roots, pale and bitter-smelling. With the vial, you have a salve's worth. At the alchemy bench, type craft healing salve.
quest|38|trigger4|action1|actor => The root ground to paste, the water drew it green, and the healing salve is sealed in the vial. Type quaff healing salve.
quest|38|trigger5|action1|actor => The root ground to paste, the water drew it green, and the healing salve is sealed in the vial. Type quaff healing salve.
quest|38|trigger6|action1|actor => The salve spreads warm through you, a slow steady mending. That is what a brew is for. Go back to Birna and type talk birna.
quest|39|rewards|actor => Falv works a leather bandolier off a peg by his fire and tosses it to you underhand, the loops already supple from years of use. The shed-proof skin of his hands pales over the knuckles as he grips. "Wear it. Any potion or firebomb you get from then on drops into it on its own, and when you quaff, the oldest potion goes first, so your brews never sit long enough to turn. You threw clean. You did not blow your own hand off. That is more than most." He nods south, where the reeds go grey. "Past the miasma the water is poison and something rules it. The firebomb formula is yours now, and a tougher brew besides. Make your own pots. You will need them down there."
quest|39|trigger0|action1|actor => Falv has told you what the marsh will try. The leech first. Go west to the Reed Beds and type attack leech.
quest|39|trigger1|action1|actor => The marsh leech goes limp in the water. First blood in the marsh. Now the firebomb. With a creature in the room, type throw firebomb.
quest|39|trigger2|action1|actor => The firebomb bursts in a gout of flame right where you aimed it. Now you feel the cost: no second trick for a few breaths. That cooldown is shared by spells and special moves too. Next, on the Sunken Path or at the Black Pool, type forage.
quest|39|trigger3|action1|actor => That is foraging the marsh: working the firm ground between the cattails for what grows there. Some days it gives little, and that is part of it. Go back to Falv and type talk falv.
quest|39|trigger4|action1|actor => The black pool's waterline is the richest ground in the marsh, even on a day it gives up little. Go back to Falv and type talk falv.
quest|40|rewards|actor => Falv hears you out with his hands held over the fire, water running off them in threads. "Gone, then. I felt the water change." He fills your pack with a brewer's stock from his own crates and tells you the mire's own renewal, willow-bark and mint and root, until the recipe settles in your head. The long labor of the marsh has settled into your body as a lasting toughness.
quest|40|trigger0|action1|actor => The spirit comes apart all at once, mud and black water and rot falling still and ordinary. A spring breaks clear through the rock behind it, and the poison drains out of the air. Climb back out to Falv at the Cattail Stand and type talk falv.
quest|41|rewards|actor => Tarn watches you come back with the unhurried attention of someone measuring whether you wasted her time. The amber of her eyes catches a hare's bolt half a field off and dismisses it. "You read the ground instead of staring at your feet. Most never learn that." She works a rolled cloak off her pack and tosses it to you. "Steppe wind cuts after dark."
quest|41|rewards|observer => Tarn looks the newcomer over, nods once, and hands across a rolled traveling cloak.
quest|41|trigger0|action1|actor => Tarn has told you what to look for. Go south to the Open Steppe and type track hare.
quest|41|trigger1|action1|actor => That is tracking: reading the ground for what passed and where it went. The skill gets better each time you use it. Next, type forage.
quest|41|trigger2|action1|actor => That is foraging: searching the scrub for what grows there. Some days your hands come up empty, and that is part of it. Go north to Scout Tarn and type talk tarn.
quest|41|trigger3|action1|actor => The sage flat rewards a patient hand, even on a day it gives up little. Go back to Scout Tarn on the Steppe Edge and type talk tarn.
quest|42|rewards|actor => Delk hears you out, then grunts, which from him is praise. The shed-proof skin of his hands shows pale as he rubs the cold from them. "Killed clean, rested rough, ate what you took. That is the whole of it." He pushes a pair of worn field boots across the stone and a scrap of waxed paper after them. "Stew recipe. A hot meal does more than cold meat. Now the bad work. South, the pack. They run that country in numbers and the alpha runs them. Come back about the pack when your nerve is up."
quest|42|rewards|observer => Delk grunts at the newcomer and hands across a pair of field boots.
quest|42|trigger0|action1|actor => Delk has set you to it. In the Thornbrake, north of his camp, type track pronghorn.
quest|42|trigger1|action1|actor => You read the ground for a pronghorn's line. Next, type attack pronghorn.
quest|42|trigger2|action1|actor => The pronghorn drops. Its meat is on the carcass. Type loot corpse.
quest|42|trigger3|action1|actor => You have the meat. Now rest rough before you cook. Type sleep.
quest|42|trigger4|action1|actor => You bed down rough and the field does its slow work. Your next command wakes you. At Delk's camp fire, type craft grilled meat.
quest|42|trigger5|action1|actor => The meat sears over the fire, salt and smoke and fat. Now eat it while it is hot. Type eat grilled meat.
quest|42|trigger6|action1|actor => A hot meal in the field is its own small victory. Go back to Delk in Hunter's Hollow and type talk delk.
quest|43|rewards|actor => Delk hears you out by the fire, then reaches behind him for a bundle of cured hide. "From the pack that tried to take you." The jerkin fits. He pushes a kit of rations, bandages and a firebomb after it, and talks you through the cut of the hide until you could sew another at any loom. The long work of the steppe has settled into you as a hunter's sharpness, eyes and instinct quicker than they were.
quest|43|trigger0|action1|actor => The alpha pack-leader shudders and goes down, and the den falls silent. The hounds that survive scatter and do not re-form. Go back to Delk in Hunter's Hollow and type talk delk.
quest|44|rewards|actor => Grieve watches the mote take your spell, and something in his mismatched eyes settles. "There. You did not reach for it. You let it go, and that is the whole of it." He takes a long staff of pale oak from the wall and sets it in your hands. It is light, and the wood seems to lean toward the work. "A focus. It will not cast for you, but it will not fight you either. Remember the three channels: the body's force, the mind's will and the heart's conviction. You loosed conviction just now. Willpower is the stat that shapes a spell, and the more of it you carry, the cleaner the fold. When you are ready, I will send you north to the grove, where Orrin teaches the holding of a casting while the world tries to knock it loose."
quest|44|rewards|observer => Grieve presses a pale oak staff into the newcomer's hands.
quest|44|trigger1|action1|actor => You gather the spell and send it at the mote. That is casting: will shaped to a purpose and let go. The mote may flicker back at you, and a second casting can scatter it, but Grieve folds a new one out of the air for the next student. Go back south to Adept Grieve in the Observatory Hall and type talk grieve.
quest|45|rewards|actor => Orrin's late-arriving outline catches up to him as he goes still. "You were hit, and the fold held anyway. That is concentration: holding on through the disturbance." He turns a palm up, and a scatter of weightless sparks gathers above it and disperses. "Here is a wider working, then: sparks. It is the weakest of the area spells, which is to say it is the first one you can trust yourself with. It touches everything in front of you at once. You loosed it from the same conviction you woke with. When you are ready, I have one more task for you, and it is the hard one."
quest|45|trigger1|action1|actor => You shape the fold with the grove pressing in on you and loose it at the creature. Now bring it down: type cast spike again until it falls.
quest|45|trigger2|action1|actor => You shape the fold with the grove pressing in on you and loose it at the creature. Now bring it down: type cast spike again until it falls.
quest|45|trigger3|action1|actor => The drift-wisp comes apart into the motes it was made of and does not gather again. Go back to Keeper Orrin in the Whispering Grove and type talk orrin.
quest|45|trigger4|action1|actor => The grove revenant folds down and is still. Go back to Keeper Orrin in the Whispering Grove and type talk orrin.
quest|46|rewards|actor => Orrin listens, and his late-arriving outline catches up to him as he goes still. "Undone. I felt the thinnest place go quiet from here." You feel the long strain of holding castings together in the open settle into you as a deeper steadiness of will. "The scabland gave you something more, whether you noticed it or not," he says, and he shows you how to turn a fold toward mending and lay it on your own wounds. You know how to heal now.
quest|46|trigger0|action1|actor => The Unfolded unravels a final time and does not refold. The thinnest place falls quiet around you. Go back to Keeper Orrin in the Whispering Grove and type talk orrin.
quest|47|rewards|actor => Wenna watches you a moment with those flat gold eyes, then nods as though settling something. "You ask straight and you listen straight. That is most of getting on with people, and all of getting on with us." She knots a small charm of plaited grass and polished bone and presses it into your hand. "Wear it where it shows. The folk will know the sign and treat you the kindlier for it." A little of her unhurried certainty seems to stay with you as she turns back to the yard. "When you are ready, I will send you on to the stones. Hale keeps them, and he has been waiting a long time to tell their story to someone who will sit still for it."
quest|47|rewards|observer => Wenna presses a small plaited charm into the newcomer's hand.
quest|47|trigger1|action1|actor => That is the in-game help, your long-term reference, more patient than any person and always to hand. The folk set their lore in stone for the same reason: so it outlasts the remembering. Go back to Elder Wenna and type talk wenna.
quest|48|rewards|actor => Hale's doubled voice settles to a single tone as he regards you. "I felt that from here, the moment his nerve went. That is rhetoric: the true word, landed where it weighs most. You have the beginnings of it." He lifts a flat strip of carved bone from among the stones and sets it in your hands. "A reckoning, the folk's whole story in the old script, small enough to carry. Read it when you have the patience. The oldest end is the part none of us can read any longer." He looks north, to where the ground rises past the ring. "There is a thing the bone only points at. When you are ready, I will send you to the one who keeps it."
quest|48|trigger1|action1|actor => Your words find the gap in his bluster and go straight through it. The fight goes out of Garrow all at once. He throws up his heavy hands, mutters a surrender and quits the green. Old Ferd lets out a breath he has been holding for days. Go south to Hale at the Stone Circle and type talk hale.
quest|49|rewards|actor => Sere listens to your account with the stillness of someone who has waited a long time to hear it, the pale shape of her skull faintly lit from within. "So it is real," she says at last, very quietly. "I have felt it under the floor for thirty years and never had the hands or the right to lift it. You did." She does not ask you to bring it to her. She seems to understand it is not a thing to be owned. "Leave it where the light can reach it. Some things are meant to be found more than once." Then, with a gravity that settles over you like a mantle: "You came to us a stranger. You leave a friend of the coulee folk, and the only living soul who has looked on the thing beneath the shrine and carried the wondering back out. Carry it well. One day, somewhere, it may come to mean more than either of us can see from here."
quest|49|trigger1|action1|actor => Your fingers find the lifted edge of a flagstone, and under it something that is not stone: cool, smooth, regular. You work it free, a disc of pale grey metal the size of a spread hand, and nothing about it belongs here. It is neither cast nor forged nor any process the folk have a word for, its face made smooth the way still water is smooth. Fine raised lines branch and rejoin across it with a cold regularity, threading inward toward a single mark pressed deep at the center: a ring with a line struck through it, the very mark the reckoning-bone carries at its oldest, deepest end. It stays cool in your warm hands. You do not understand it, and you are fairly certain no one in the coulee does. It feels less like something the folk made and lost than like something that was already here when they came, waiting under the floor for a hand to lift it. You set it back in its bed of stone, where the light can reach it.
quest|49|trigger1|action2|actor => Go back to Sere in the Old Shrine and type talk sere.
quest|50|rewards|actor => Iden watches your last stone fly down the range and gives a single nod. "There. A sling readies itself while your eye is still on the mark, so the only thing you have to think about is the mark. And you have the other half already: a shot from cover lands like nothing else, and it works once, because afterward they know where you are. The eye is the thing that matters now, the eye and never the arm. Keep the sling and the shot. They are yours." She tips her head north, toward the canyon mouth. "When you are ready, I will send you up to Bryn. He will show you how to put a shot into something a whole room away, before it ever knows you are there."
quest|50|rewards|observer => Marksman Iden nods as the newcomer's last stone flies down the range.
quest|50|trigger1|action1|actor => Iden has your measure. Ready the sling: type equip sling. If it is already in your hand, first use remove sling.
quest|50|trigger2|action1|actor => The sling settles in your hand. Go to the Long Terrace, east of the Firing Range, and type fire butt.
quest|50|trigger3|action1|actor => The stone leaves the sling and flies at the butt. Your hand has already found another. Iden calls down the range: "Now again, from where it cannot see you coming. Type sneak."
quest|50|trigger4|action1|actor => You settle out of sight behind the butts. Type fire butt and see what a shot is worth when nothing is expecting it. If the butt is down, wait a moment for a fresh butt.
quest|50|trigger5|action1|actor => That shot left from cover. Go west to Marksman Iden and type talk iden.
quest|51|rewards|actor => Bryn's outline doubles for a moment as he turns to you, then settles. "You felt it, then. A shot across the slot brings the thing it was aimed at straight up the slot at you, so the cross-room shot is never free. You buy a reach, and you pay for it with a fight. Worth it, when you choose the ground." He works a compact crossbow loose from the rock behind him and hands it over with a case of bolts. "Heavier than a sling, and it hits like it. Above us is the overlook, and on it a bowmaster named Skell, who has made this whole canyon a killing field from up there. Ready the crossbow before you climb. When you have the nerve, the chimney at the canyon's head goes up to him."
quest|51|rewards|observer => Scout Bryn passes the newcomer a compact crossbow and a case of bolts.
quest|51|trigger1|action1|actor => Your shot goes out at the canyon scout. Hold your ground in the Narrows. When the scout reaches you, type fire scout until it falls.
quest|51|trigger2|action1|actor => The canyon scout drops. That is the whole of it: reach out, then stand your ground. Go back to Scout Bryn in the Canyon Mouth and type talk bryn.
quest|52|rewards|actor => Bryn hears you out, and his doubled outline settles. "Off the high stand. Then the canyon is ours, and the band has lost the ground that let it rule us." From the raider cache his scouts carried down, he hands you a full hunting bow and ammunition enough to keep it fed. You feel the long work of the terraces and the canyon settle into you as a keenness of eye. Distances come quicker now, and the right instant to loose is just there when you reach for it. The whole coulee lies open behind you, every spoke of it walked and won, and past the rim the wider scablands wait.
quest|52|rewards|observer => Scout Bryn hands the newcomer a hunting bow from the raider cache.
quest|52|trigger0|action1|actor => Bowmaster Skell goes off the overlook and does not rise. The high ground is yours, and the canyon below falls quiet. Go back down to Scout Bryn at the Canyon Mouth and type talk bryn.
quest|53|rewards|actor => Garve counts a few coins into your palm with his good hand. "The wash is quiet again. Come back when it is not. It never stays quiet long."
quest|53|trigger0|action1|actor => One scout down. Now the squatter: from Squatter's Hollow, go east to the Cracked Cistern and type attack squatter.
quest|53|trigger1|action1|actor => The squatter drops. Go back to Garve in Squatter's Hollow and type talk garve for your pay.
quest|54|rewards|actor => Ovell turns a coin over his knuckles before he hands it to you. "Still sharp. The iron knows a practiced hand. Come back when you want to keep it that way."
quest|54|rewards|observer => Ovell hands <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> a few coins with a slow, approving nod.
quest|54|trigger0|action1|actor => The work rings clean off the anvil. Go back to Ovell in the Collapsed Cut and type talk ovell.
quest|55|rewards|actor => Falv sniffs the empty bottle and nods. "Fresh. The marsh does not care how long ago you learned, only whether your salve is fresh." He presses a few coins into your hand.
quest|55|rewards|observer => Falv sniffs an empty bottle and nods at <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi>.
quest|55|trigger0|action1|actor => The brew came off the bench clean, steeped to the right color. Type quaff healing salve, or quaff whatever you made.
quest|55|trigger1|action1|actor => The brew came off the bench clean, steeped to the right color. Type quaff healing salve, or quaff whatever you made.
quest|55|trigger2|action1|actor => The brew does what it promised. Go back to Falv at the Cattail Stand and type talk falv.
quest|56|rewards|actor => Delk listens to the run and grunts. "Clean kill, eyes open, and the land worked after it." He hands over a few coins. "The fringe teaches you different things each pass."
quest|56|trigger0|action1|actor => The pronghorn goes down clean. Now, on the Open Steppe, type forage.
quest|56|trigger1|action1|actor => You work the steppe for what it gives. Some days that is little, and the run still counts. Go back to Delk and type talk delk.
quest|57|rewards|actor => Orrin nods, and for a moment every edge of him arrives on time. "The fold held clean. They always drift back in. Come back when the watch slips again."
quest|57|rewards|observer => Keeper Orrin nods to <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi>, and the grove settles, as if it approves of the stillness.
quest|57|trigger0|action1|actor => The drift-wisp unravels and is gone. Go back north to Keeper Orrin and type talk orrin.
quest|58|rewards|actor => Sere listens with her eyes closed. "Not quite what they said last time. Very old places keep speaking, and the words shift with the listener. Come again when you have the patience for it."
quest|58|rewards|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> tells Hermit Sere what the stones said, and she listens with her eyes closed.
quest|58|trigger0|action1|actor => The stones give up a little more than they did before. It is not much, but it is something. The old mark, unchanged and patient, catches your eye again. Go back to Hermit Sere in the Old Shrine and type talk sere.
quest|59|rewards|actor => Bryn gives a single nod. "Good reach. Stood when it came. Come and find me when the eye starts to drift. It always drifts."
quest|59|rewards|observer => Scout Bryn gives the newcomer a single nod.
quest|59|trigger0|action1|actor => Your shot goes out across the slot. Hold your ground in the Narrows. When the scout reaches you, type fire scout until it falls.
quest|59|trigger1|action1|actor => The scout drops. Shot placed, fight finished. Go back south to Scout Bryn in the Canyon Mouth and type talk bryn.
quest|60|rewards|actor => The guard breaks the seal, scans the packet, and marks the gate ledger with a short nod. The brass token he pressed into your hand is stamped with the tower and three waves of New Plymouth: the mark of a courier who carried the capital's word the length of the road.
quest|60|rewards|observer => The East Gate guard takes the sealed packet, checks its seal against the gate ledger, and logs it in.
quest|61|rewards|actor => Pemberton listens to the whole of it, then lets out a breath she seems to have been holding for a week. "Both of them. Then I can tell my lodgers the road north is walkable again and not be lying." She counts coin from the strongbox without haggling for once, and presses a salve into your hand on top of it. "For the next set of bruises. You will have them, doing work like this. There is always a seat by my fire for you."
quest|61|rewards|observer => Goodwife Pemberton settles a purse into the traveller's hand with the air of a woman whose trade just started breathing again.
quest|61|trigger0|action1|actor => The hedgerow bandit folds into the ditch he ambushed from and does not get up. One of the road's two is done. The Reach-Touched still haunts the Empty Reach to the north.
quest|61|trigger1|action1|actor => The Reach-Touched shudders, goes still, and is just a body on the stones. The road north is clear of both now. Carry the word back to Pemberton at the Lake & Ladle.
quest|61|trigger2|action1|actor => The Reach-Touched shudders, goes still, and is just a body on the stones. One of the road's two is done. The hedgerow bandit still lies hidden in the reeds at the Mire Cutoff, southwest of the Lake & Ladle.
quest|61|trigger3|action1|actor => The hedgerow bandit folds into the ditch he ambushed from and does not get up. The road is clear of both now. Carry the word back to Pemberton at the Lake & Ladle.
quest|62|rewards|actor => Tamsin works the pole-callus on her palm with a thumb and looks south toward the reeds, where nothing is moving for once. "That thing put two of my passengers in the mud this season and near cost me a third. It is a kinder crossing without it." She counts out coin and tucks a small stoppered vial in on top. "Antivenom. Keep it. The reeds breed more than one of those, and the next might find you before you find it."
quest|62|rewards|observer => Tamsin Reed presses coin and a small vial into the traveller's hand, glancing south toward the quiet reeds.
quest|62|trigger0|action1|actor => The marsh adder coils, strikes once at nothing, and goes limp in the reeds. The south approach is quiet. Carry the word back to Tamsin at the ford landing.
quest|63|rewards|actor => The matter settles the way the docks settle things: quietly, and for good. Hewd will answer for the difference between his two columns, and Teo goes back on the board in the morning. The dockfolk will hear who sorted it, and down here that is worth more than coin, though there is coin in it too.
quest|63|rewards|observer => Word moves along the wharves in the way it does, and more than one dockhand gives the traveller a short, respectful nod.
quest|63|trigger0|action2|actor => The proud board lifts with a little persuasion. In the gap beneath, wrapped in oilcloth, lies a small tally-book, and a glance inside is enough. Two columns of numbers for every shipment: the manifest count on the left, the real one on the right. Foreman Hewd has been skimming the difference for a long time, and the shortage he reported was Teo's only by his choosing.
quest|63|trigger0|action3|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> works a loose floorboard free and pockets something wrapped in oilcloth.
quest|63|trigger1|action0|actor => One floorboard sits a little proud of its neighbors. You could work it loose, but prying up another man's floor without a reason is a fast way to find trouble you came here to avoid.
quest|63|trigger2|action2|actor => The proud board lifts with a little persuasion. In the gap beneath, wrapped in oilcloth, lies a small tally-book, and a glance inside is enough. Two columns of numbers for every shipment: the manifest count on the left, the real one on the right. Foreman Hewd has been skimming the difference for a long time, and the shortage he reported was Teo's only by his choosing.
quest|63|trigger2|action3|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> works a loose floorboard free and pockets something wrapped in oilcloth.
quest|63|trigger3|action0|actor => One floorboard sits a little proud of its neighbors. You could work it loose, but prying up another man's floor without a reason is a fast way to find trouble you came here to avoid.
quest|63|trigger4|action1|actor => You lift the board again. Hewd kept a fair copy as well as his working book, and it is still there in the oilcloth. You take it.
quest|63|trigger4|action2|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> lifts a loose floorboard and takes something wrapped in oilcloth.
quest|63|trigger5|action1|actor => You lift the board again. Hewd kept a fair copy as well as his working book, and it is still there in the oilcloth. You take it.
quest|63|trigger5|action2|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> lifts a loose floorboard and takes something wrapped in oilcloth.
quest|65|rewards|actor => Coll turns the cold gray lump over in his sweeper's hands, and for once he has nothing to say for a long moment. "Older than the city. Under the city. And it washes up in my gutters when the rain's hard enough to loosen it." He pockets it carefully. "The bookseller wasn't wrong to go quiet. Keep this between us. The sort who'd want to know about a buried city aren't the sort I'd want knowing I found it. But you did right by an old sweeper, and the quarter remembers that."
quest|65|rewards|observer => Coll the sweeper closes his hand around a cold gray lump and, for once, says nothing at all.
quest|65|trigger0|action2|actor => You set a hand to the seam and the cold of it goes straight to the bone: not the cold of stone but something older and more patient. A lump comes loose in your fingers, fist-sized and far too heavy: the same gray material Coll finds in fragments, here in the mass, seamed through worked stone that was old before New Plymouth's first wall was laid. The rain loosens pieces of it and the gutters carry them up to the streets above. This is the source.
quest|65|trigger0|action3|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> works a heavy gray lump loose from a seam in the old stonework.
quest|65|trigger1|action0|actor => A seam of cold gray material runs through the old stone. Not quarried rock, something stranger and far older. You could work a piece loose, but without a reason it is just a curiosity in the dark.
quest|65|trigger2|action2|actor => You set a hand to the seam and the cold of it goes straight to the bone: not the cold of stone but something older and more patient. A lump comes loose in your fingers, fist-sized and far too heavy: the same gray material Coll finds in fragments, here in the mass, seamed through worked stone that was old before New Plymouth's first wall was laid. The rain loosens pieces of it and the gutters carry them up to the streets above. This is the source.
quest|65|trigger2|action3|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> works a heavy gray lump loose from a seam in the old stonework.
quest|65|trigger3|action0|actor => A seam of cold gray material runs through the old stone. Not quarried rock, something stranger and far older. You could work a piece loose, but without a reason it is just a curiosity in the dark.
quest|65|trigger4|action1|actor => You work another lump of the gray material loose from the seam. It is just as cold, and just as heavy.
quest|65|trigger4|action2|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> works a heavy gray lump loose from a seam in the old stonework.
quest|65|trigger5|action1|actor => You work another lump of the gray material loose from the seam. It is just as cold, and just as heavy.
quest|65|trigger5|action2|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> works a heavy gray lump loose from a seam in the old stonework.
quest|66|rewards|actor => Teels will be stable, for now. Ysolde was clear: the purge holds until the craving comes back, and the craving comes back while the source is still running. The wrapper is gone but the smell stays with you. The docks know where the Bloom comes from, or someone on them does.
quest|66|rewards|observer => The traveller looks up from a quiet exchange with the look of someone who has just learned something they cannot unlearn.
quest|67|rewards|actor => The trade is broken, for now. The constable took the case file and his jaw was set when he read it. Deren stays untouched. The bloodline office is a wall you cannot move with evidence. But the supply stops, and that buys Teels a chance. One life you could reach.
quest|67|rewards|observer => A wharfside quiet settles over the traveller, the look of someone who has done what could be done.
quest|68|trigger2|action2|actor => A floorboard by the cot sits proud of its neighbors. Beneath it, wrapped in oilcloth against the damp, is a torn quarter of a survey in an old, exact hand: Edvar's work, the map Toby said was hidden here. You ease it free and pocket it.
quest|68|trigger2|action3|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> works a loose floorboard free and lifts something wrapped in oilcloth.
quest|68|trigger3|action0|actor => One floorboard near the cot sits a little proud of the rest. Prying up the floor of an occupied workshop without a reason is the kind of thing that ends a welcome before it starts. You leave it.
quest|68|trigger4|action0|actor => The cooper's guild mark, a stave and hammer, is painted beside the door, the paint cracked and lifting. Re-cut, it would tell any clerk this is a working shop. Whether that happens is the circle's to decide, and Orin speaks for the circle.
quest|68|trigger5|action0|actor => The cooper's guild mark, a stave and hammer, is painted beside the door in faded paint. Re-cutting it would be a real act with real consequences. You do not yet have a reason to.
quest|68|trigger6|action2|actor => A floorboard by the cot sits proud of its neighbors. Beneath it, wrapped in oilcloth against the damp, is a torn quarter of a survey in an old, exact hand: Edvar's work, the map Toby said was hidden here. You ease it free and pocket it.
quest|68|trigger6|action3|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> works a loose floorboard free and lifts something wrapped in oilcloth.
quest|68|trigger7|action0|actor => One floorboard near the cot sits a little proud of the rest. Prying up the floor of an occupied workshop without a reason is the kind of thing that ends a welcome before it starts. You leave it.
quest|68|trigger8|action1|actor => The board is loose and the space beneath it is empty. You already have Edvar's survey. Take it to Orin.
quest|68|trigger9|action1|actor => The board is loose and the space beneath it is empty. You already have Edvar's survey. Take it to Orin.
quest|68|trigger10|action0|actor => The cooper's guild mark, a stave and hammer, is painted beside the door, the paint cracked and lifting. Re-cut, it would tell any clerk this is a working shop. Whether that happens is the circle's to decide, and Orin speaks for the circle.
quest|68|trigger11|action0|actor => The cooper's guild mark, a stave and hammer, is painted beside the door in faded paint. Re-cutting it would be a real act with real consequences. You do not yet have a reason to.
quest|69|rewards|actor => Dross lays the rubbing and the reading side by side and goes very quiet, which for him is remarkable. "It holds," he says. "Every line of it holds." He has a proof now that no honest examiner could dismiss, and he is, you both understand, a man no one with power has ever been obliged to honestly examine. Still. It is known now, and you are one of the few who know it.
quest|69|rewards|observer => The traveller has the look of someone who has read something that cannot be un-read.
quest|69|trigger0|action2|actor => You press paper to the processional relief and work charcoal across it. The figures come up under your hand, and the longer you look, the less devotional they seem. Each hand is positioned too precisely to be art. Read along the row, they are a sequence: a number, set into stone by someone who wanted it kept where it could not be edited out.
quest|69|trigger0|action3|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> takes a careful charcoal rubbing of the old processional reliefs.
quest|69|trigger1|action0|actor => The processional figures are very old, older somehow than the plaque that names them. Their hands are oddly placed. Without a reason to study them you move on.
quest|69|trigger4|action1|actor => You press a fresh sheet to the processional relief and work the charcoal across it again. The hands come up in the same precise row, the same counted sequence.
quest|69|trigger4|action2|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> takes a careful charcoal rubbing of the old processional reliefs.
quest|70|rewards|actor => Orin turns the rubbing toward the lamp and is quiet for a long moment. "So it is really down there," he says. "The painting copied this, and the cipher counts toward it, and now there is a rubbing of the thing itself. Gritta found it, you stood under it, and I will see it reaches the people who can hold it." He files it away with a care that is its own kind of reverence. You are, without anything being said, part of the quiet now.
quest|70|rewards|observer => The old bookseller gives the traveller a slow nod, the kind that settles something unspoken between them.
quest|70|trigger0|action2|actor => You press paper to the underside of the lintel and bring the symbol up in charcoal: four concentric rings, eight points at equal intervals, cut by someone who drew it before they carved it. The colony arrived here, found this, and wrote itself into the founding record as first. The rubbing in your hands says otherwise, quietly, the way the stone does.
quest|70|trigger0|action3|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> takes a careful rubbing of the symbol carved beneath the buried lintel.
quest|70|trigger1|action0|actor => The symbol on the lintel's underside is clean and deliberate: rings and eight points, cut to be read by someone passing beneath. Without a reason to record it, you only look.
quest|70|trigger2|action0|actor => The seam of gray material runs along the flood line, wider here than in the galleries, smooth where the black water works it, taking no mark, no wear. It does not belong to any stone the colony has a name for. It was here before the canal, before the quarter, before the founding the city teaches.
quest|71|rewards|actor => Ostry reads the page once, folds it, and puts it somewhere you do not see. "I cannot fight them with this," she says, "and I am not fool enough to try. But I can let the right person know I have it, and tomorrow my deposit comes back and my permit clears, and nobody says why. That is how it works down here." She presses a blade into your hands before you can decline it. "You will get more use from it than from my thanks."
quest|71|rewards|observer => Dame Ostry clasps the traveller's forearm once, hard and brief, the nearest thing she has to ceremony.
quest|71|trigger2|action2|actor => The torn scrap on the floor reads "before the permit clears", and the page it tore from is still on the table among the cup rings, slid half under a ledger-board. You take it: a column of quarterly sums against vendor names, every figure routed up to one unnamed account. It does not prove a crime. It proves exactly where the money goes, and who waits on whom.
quest|71|trigger2|action3|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> palms a page from the table among the cup rings.
quest|71|trigger3|action0|actor => A torn scrap on the floor carries four words, "before the permit clears", in a careful hand. There is more to it somewhere, but lifting papers from this room uninvited, before you know whose they are, is the kind of mistake the Gilt Threshold is built to punish.
quest|71|trigger5|action1|actor => The ledger-board is still on the table among the cup rings, and another page of the same column has worked loose beneath it. You take it: the same quarterly sums, routed up to the same unnamed account.
quest|71|trigger5|action2|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> palms a page from the table among the cup rings.
quest|72|rewards|actor => Word of the settling runs the valley before you have even left the lane. Whatever was decided, the shouting at the Golden Bough will quiet now, and that alone has earned you a place at its hearth.
quest|72|rewards|observer => The traveller has the settled look of someone who has untangled a thing that stayed knotted for a long time.
quest|72|trigger0|action1|actor => You climb the slide and look it over. A whole span of the old aqueduct lies buried under fallen rock and slumped earth. Above it the water stands brimming and blocked; below it the bed runs dry all the way down to the farms. Neither man cut this channel. The hill did. It is far too much stone for one back, but a valley turned out with ropes could clear it in a day, and then the water would run down to both farms at once. Hesper at the Golden Bough could call them out.
quest|72|trigger0|action2|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> climbs over the slide of fallen stone across the old aqueduct, studying it.
quest|72|trigger1|action1|actor => The old water-right is here among the ceremony rolls, dated and witnessed in a careful hand: the head-gate share was set to feed both holdings, turn and turn about. By the letter of it, Ayres has taken more than his due for years. It is not a kind answer. It is the true one, and it favours Fenn. Hesper at the Golden Bough would know what reading it aloud would do to the valley.
quest|73|rewards|actor => "Three records, three hands, sixty years apart, and they agree on the one thing the official account denies. There was a fourth. Someone unmade it. Not the water: the memory of it." Quist folds a clean sheet and presses it into your hands. "A fair copy, with the fourth channel drawn back where it belongs. Take it. And if you mean to follow this further, the answer is not in any archive of ours. It is under the temple, in the stone the founders built upon and would not explain. Go carefully. Some questions are settled by people who would prefer they stay that way."
quest|73|rewards|observer => Quist presses a folded sheet into the visitor's hands, talking low and urgent.
quest|73|trigger0|action1|actor => You study the damaged chart past its water-stain. At the junction, plain under the ruined ink, a fourth channel is drawn: narrow, distinct, running off to the southwest, no mere smear of current. One of the three records Quist sent you to find.
quest|73|trigger0|action2|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> studies the bookseller's water-damaged old chart with new attention.
quest|73|trigger1|action0|actor => A water-damaged old harbor chart on the bookseller's wall, half its detail lost to a stain. Old, and odd at the junction, but you have no particular reason to study it closely.
quest|73|trigger2|action1|actor => Tallis's oldest charts show the same fourth channel, struck out in some copies and re-marked in others, across sixty years of hands that could not agree whether it belonged. The disagreement is consistent. Two records now, and they were never copied from each other.
quest|73|trigger2|action2|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> pores over the oldest charts in Tallis's stall.
quest|73|trigger3|action0|actor => The oldest charts in the stall, a few showing the river-junction with more channels than the current maps carry. A curiosity of the copying trade, and nothing you have a reason to pursue.
quest|73|trigger4|action1|actor => The hall's own map carries it too: a fourth channel pencilled into the margin in an older hand, half struck through, the note beside it admitting that the surveyors could not agree. The city's own record, hung in public, says the count was once in dispute. Three independent records. Time to report back to Quist.
quest|73|trigger4|action2|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> examines the marginal note on the great hall map closely.
quest|73|trigger5|action0|actor => An old marginal annotation on the civic map: a fourth channel, struck through, with a note that the surveyors could not agree. The staff have stopped seeing it.
quest|74|rewards|actor => The Undercroft kept its threshold and gave up its secret: there was a fourth, struck from the sky and the count and the record, and the temple was raised on the place that remembered. What unmade it is not here. The rubbing in your memory points away from the Confluence entirely, north and older, to wherever the sky was changed. That road is for another day.
quest|74|trigger0|action1|actor => You read the building-ledger past its careful columns. It accounts for every stone of the temple's raising, except the lowest courses, which it simply assumes, as though the foundation were a thing received rather than built. The first of the three records.
quest|74|trigger0|action2|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> reads the open building-ledger with sudden attention.
quest|74|trigger1|action0|actor => An old construction ledger open on a reading-stand, meticulous and dry. Without a reason to read it closely, it is only an account book.
quest|74|trigger2|action1|actor => The consecration-record sets out the Founders' dedication of the temple, and its own wording betrays it: they consecrated the site, a word that assumes something already stood here to be made holy. The second record agrees with the first.
quest|74|trigger2|action2|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> reads the open consecration-record closely.
quest|74|trigger3|action0|actor => The temple's consecration-record, open on its stand in the Chapter House. A formal dedication in old script, nothing you have reason to parse word by word.
quest|74|trigger4|action1|actor => The mason's survey is the plainest of the three: the lower courses of this corridor are older work, it notes, cut and laid by hands the temple's own records do not name. Three records, three different rooms, one conclusion. Time to report to Cael.
quest|74|trigger4|action2|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> examines the old mason's survey framed in the corridor.
quest|74|trigger5|action0|actor => A mason's survey-note framed on the corridor wall, marking the stonework's courses. Technical, and old. You have no particular reason to study it.
quest|74|trigger7|action2|actor => You read the carving the way the mason's survey taught you to read stone. Four rings, cut with an instrument's care, where the temple's teaching keeps to three. The temple did not miscount. It chose a count, and built three hundred years on the choice, and set its floor over the wall that remembers otherwise. There was a fourth. The sky the Founders found was not the sky we are taught. You take a rubbing of it, proof in soft black line, and the dark keeps the rest of its counsel. Whatever unmade the fourth, the stone does not say. That answer is somewhere else.
quest|74|trigger7|action3|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> takes a careful rubbing from the great carving on the chamber wall.
quest|74|trigger8|action0|actor => A vast carving of the night sky in nested rings, cut into the chamber's far wall by a very old hand. Without a reason to count them closely, it is only a beautiful, weathered thing in the dark.
quest|75|rewards|actor => You carry a retired surveyor's directions to a place he would not name. The road runs east into the highland country, older and stranger than the university's quiet maps. Whatever Reth saw out there and chose not to write down is still out there, waiting in the broken hills. That climb is for another day.
quest|75|trigger0|action1|actor => You read the survey the way someone looking for what is not said would read it. The site is classified as a mineral deposit in three lines. A survey of that site -- elevations, material samples, seasonal access -- would ordinarily run to a page or more. This one does not. The entry is formal and correct and stops exactly where the detail should get louder. Reth saw something out there, and he filed a paper that buries it. Time to take this back to Brennan.
quest|75|trigger0|action2|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> reads the thin filed survey with sudden, careful attention.
quest|75|trigger1|action0|actor => An old survey filed under the eastern country, dry and technical. Without a reason to read it closely, it is only a brief, dull entry.
quest|75|trigger3|action4|actor => You take the marked map from the table — Reth's hand, annotated in the close careful script of a man who does not waste ink. A route east into the highland country, a circled waymark, elevation ticks that tell you what kind of ground you are going into. No name for what is at the end of it. Whatever Reth saw out there he would not write down, and he has not written it down now — but the route is exact, and the final mark is deliberate, and it is enough. The thread runs east.
quest|75|trigger3|action5|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> takes the surveyor's marked map from the table.
quest|75|trigger4|action0|actor => A retired surveyor's old papers spread across the table — terrain charts and route sketches in a close, careful hand. Without his leave they are not yours to take, and they say little to a stranger at the window.
quest|76|rewards|actor => Brennan turns the woken disc to the light and watches the lines keep it. "A father's work, finished by a stranger, in the cottage he left to chase it." He gives it back. What it opens waits east, in the broken country, behind a door in the buried face.
quest|76|rewards|observer => Brennan turns a grey disc to the light and hands it back.
quest|76|trigger0|action0|actor => You work the loose stone free of its neighbors. It grinds aside and shows a small cavity in the wall behind it. Inside, a folded letter lies against the back of the hollow, hidden there on purpose.
quest|76|trigger2|action1|actor => Between the last pages of the journal lies a grey disc, cool and dead in the hand, the twin of the one you woke. You carry it away.
quest|76|trigger3|action1|actor => Pressed between the last pages of the journal on the table lies a disc of pale grey metal: cool, too smooth, heavier than its size. Fine raised lines thread across its face to a ring struck through with a line. You take it.
quest|76|trigger3|action2|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> lifts something grey from between the pages of a journal and pockets it.
quest|76|trigger4|action1|actor => You sit at the cold table and read the man's life backward.
Years of it: a hand that starts careful and turns driven, the
same questions put a hundred ways to one buried thing far to
the east. Something made, he is certain, and old past any
reckoning, and wrong in a way he never quite sets down in
words. He calls it only the thing. The ring struck through with
a line is inked in every margin, worried at like a sore tooth.
Then, near the end, the part you came for without knowing it:
a method, worked out slow and sure across many pages, for
waking the grey disc that is its key. Light, held over it at
the marked hearth. The last line is not about the thing at
all. It is a name, set down once and gently, as if to keep one
soft thing safe. Maren. He went east to finish this. He did not
come back to her. At the marked hearth, type cast glow.

quest|76|trigger4|action2|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> reads a long while at the cottage table.
quest|76|trigger5|action2|actor => You set the grey disc into the cut center of the hearthstone and hold the glow over it, as his method says. The lines warm, and the mark at the center wakes.
quest|76|trigger6|action1|actor => His method wants the disc itself. Between the last pages of the journal lies one, pale grey, cool and dead in the hand. You carry it to the hearth.
quest|76|trigger7|action3|actor => You do as the journal says. You set the disc into the cut
center of the hearthstone, where the marks draw inward to a
single point, and you hold the soft glow over it, patient and
exact, the way a driven man learned alone and wrote down so a
stranger might one day do this right. For a long moment,
nothing. Then the grey face warms under your fingers, not with
your warmth but its own. The fine raised lines drink the light
and keep it, holding a glow a half-breath past when it should
fade, and the ring-struck mark at the center wakes and steadies,
sure of itself now, sure of where it belongs. The disc is a key,
and it knows its door: east, in the broken country, in the
buried face he gave his years to. His work, done at last, by a
stranger's hand in the cottage he left to chase it. And a name
comes to you off the last page, unbidden. Maren. He kept her,
all the way to the end of himself. You hope, wherever she is,
she never learns how far he went. Brennan will want to hear of
this. Go back to his office in Greenford and type talk brennan.

quest|76|trigger7|action4|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> holds a soft glow over the marked hearth, and the air goes briefly strange.
quest|77|rewards|actor => You know now. It sits in you like a swallowed stone. The sky will never look the same, and neither will the blessed, and neither will you. Be careful who you tell.
quest|77|trigger0|action2|actor => You stand among the stones and let the light find them, and one
by one they wake — a slow inner glow, a drift of moving marks —
and though you cannot read the tongue, the stones do not need you
to. They show. They lay it out plainly, the whole of it, in
light and in shape, and you understand it the way you understand
a face, all at once and without wanting to.

They show a dark with no floor and no walls, and points of cold
fire strewn across it past all counting, and — falling through
that dark on a long spear of fire — this. This place, whole once,
a vessel. Not built by any hand of the world. Built to cross the
impossible black, and full of people. People who chose to come.
Who left somewhere behind and set out across a distance the mind
slides off of, meaning to make a home on the green world below.
Gaius. Here. This ground you were born to. They came to it. On
purpose. From somewhere else.

The stones show the landing, and the sickness after. A fine thing
in the soil and the water and the air of this world, waiting,
native to it — and the strangers had no armour against it. It
took them. It changed them, root and blood, into something the
world would learn to call blessed. But there was nothing chosen
in it, and nothing holy. The Chrysalis was here before them. The
blessing is a catching thing. It is the world's own fever, and
they were only the first to burn with it.

The stones show the few it could not touch. Not favoured. Not
spared by any will above. Only made, by the blind luck of how
they were built inside, so that the fever found no purchase in
them — and their children after, and theirs, carrying that dumb
accident down the long years until it wore the shape of divine
right. The bloodline. Their immunity was never grace. It was the
cruelest kind of chance, and a whole world knelt to it.

And the stones show one thing more, and hold it, so you cannot
look away. The vessel was not alone. It came in company. The
stones show three more, still whole, still waiting, hung in the
high dark above the green world and turning there, patient, for a
very long time. You have looked up at them all your life. Everyone
has. On clear nights you counted them and called them by the old
names and never once knew you were looking at ships. The moons.
The moons are ships. And they are still full.

The light drifts and settles, and the stones go quiet, having
told you everything. You do not feel wiser. You feel like someone
who has been handed a weight and told it is theirs now, forever.

quest|77|trigger0|action3|observer => <ansi fg="username">Aliceia</ansi> stands motionless before the wall of moving light, and for a long moment does not seem to breathe.
quest|77|trigger1|action0|actor => They are only stones again now, dark until the light finds them — but you know what they hold, and you know it holds you. The crossing, the fever, the luck, the waiting lights. You have read it. You will always have read it.
quest|1000000|rewards|actor => Congratulations, here's some stuff!
quest|1000000|rewards|observer => A Generic Quest has been completed!
